Third-party components in or used by HakiOS
(full table with origins and status: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md; compliance notes: COMPLIANCE.md)

In the repository:

- XNU (Apple): the kernel sources are fetched by xnu/apply.sh from github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu;
  our patch and files are a derivative work under the Apple Public Source License 2.0 (LICENSE.APSL).
- libdeflate (Eric Biggers), xnu/files/bsd/miscfs/apfs/libdeflate/: MIT, see its COPYING.
- mkbootimg.py (Android Open Source Project), devices/poco-x5-pro/prebuilt/mkbootimg.py: Apache License 2.0.
- Mu-Silicium / Project Mu (Project Silicium, Microsoft and contributors): devices/poco-x5-pro/uefi/ holds a
  patch and files against it; their license applies to the derived parts (BSD-2-Clause-Patent).
- UEFI driver binaries of the phone's own firmware (devices/poco-x5-pro/uefi/files/Binaries/redwood/) are
  the vendor's (Qualcomm/Xiaomi) and are not in this repository: each user extracts them from their own
  phone's xbl.img with UEFIReader. Only their README (the list of patches applied to them) is kept.

- the FocalTech touch firmware, xnu/files/bsd/dev/hakios.focaltech_fw.h: the touch vendor's;
  generated from a device blob, redistribution terms "to verify" (THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md).

- the Wi-Fi driver: Linux's ath11k (BSD-3-Clause-Clear) and FreeBSD's LinuxKPI headers (BSD-2-Clause) are
  fetched by tools/mk-ath11k.sh at pinned releases and built on our layer wifi/lx (MIT); only the layer is here.

- ios-flame (Pixel 4 port, github.com/NWylynko/ios-flame, a fork of dipa-studio/ios-flame): parts of the
  WCN3990 Wi-Fi bring-up of the POCO X3 Pro (xnu/files/bsd/dev/vayu_wifi_htc_connect.c, vayu_wifi_scan.c,
  vayu_wifi_sta.c, vayu_wifi_wmi.c and their headers in xnu/files/bsd/sys/) are ported from its
  phone/wifi/radio.c (commit 745c4341). MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 dipa-studio; each of those files carries
  the notice.
- Other HakiOS ports: vayu_scm.c follows the single SCM lock of the Redmi K20 Pro port (hackios_Raphael, commit
  13145c3066); the idea, no code. Code taken from another fork of HakiOS names the fork, branch and commit in the
  file's head and is listed here; those forks are under HakiOS's own licences (APSL 2.0 for the kernel, MIT
  for the rest):
  - oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel (upstream), main: HFS Plus built into the kernel and virtio_blk=2 (83aceb83817c,
    7ef54e774d32; xnu/hfs/), the hakios-metal driver, the AIR frontend in tools/mesa/air and the ir3 patches in
    tools/mesa/metal (63fc2b4633ba).
  - telegdyd/ios-vayu, vayu-dev: HFS Plus as the data volume (74cfdfa7d258, ec38881a572c, 274f9827f52f:
    /dev/ufs_var, userland/src/var_hfs.h, devices/poco-x3-pro/tools/var-volume.sh), loader 2.5's standalone start,
    layout block and staged boot image (546ac05ab957, 8054280162b9, 86984b16b016; xnuloader/loader.c,
    userland/src/flash_stage.*, devices/poco-x3-pro/tools/standalone.sh and darwin-install.sh, 56f0a3adbd41), the
    A640 port of hakios-metal, the Metal programs and docs/metal-*.md (061e5a82d023; bd98a330786f for the kernel's
    plug-in names).
  - Scion-Project/scion-kernel, main: exitlog= (a40a96524a51, bsd/kern/kern_sig.c) and systrace_log=
    (8042def0c06d, osfmk/arm64/user_exception_trace.c).
  - xreactx/hakios-xnu-kernel, oneplus-6t-upstream: vayu_bt_baud= (0e5e7bd6a05c), vayu_gnss_v02= (12d310ec3b2e),
    userland/src/gnssd.m and inject_loc.c (12d310ec3b2e, e86c96b9ada8).
  - janhurn9400/hackios-xnu-kernel, renoir: vayu_bt_baud= and BT_AUDIO=1 (7287928f164b).
  - telegdyd/hakios-xnu-kernel, negroni-dev, and kiwiiiii-eth/hakios-xnu-kernel, fajita: vayu_wifi_bounds= and
    vayu_wifi_snr= (b4c39cc65b12; d82116fb9050, 68594340fc87; bsd/dev/hakios.apple80211.c).
  - adelholzener69/hakios-xnu-kernel-raphael, raphael: wire_limit= (3233e8371422, userland/src/init.c).
- The Metal plug-in of vayu-dev and upstream (HakiosMetalCA.m) is not here: it was begun from vcvkk/darwin-redwood,
  which states no licence, and waits for its author's permission (THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md).
- Mu-Silicium's vayuPkg (Project Silicium): devices/poco-x3-pro/uefi/ fetches it at a pinned commit (BASE) and
  lays the XNU hook of devices/poco-x5-pro/uefi/ over it; BSD-2-Clause-Patent. Its device tree for the phone,
  devices/poco-x3-pro/prebuilt/device-tree.dtb, is compiled from GPL-2.0 Linux sources (to verify: see
  tools/provenance.allow).

Fetched at build time, never committed:

- HFS Plus (Apple, hfs-627.100.6, APSL 2.0): xnu/hfs/hfs.sh fetches it from github.com/apple-oss-distributions/hfs
  for xnu/apply.sh, as XNU itself; xnu/hfs/hfs.patch is this port's change to it.

- the iOS 16.5 IPSW (Apple): the user space of the system image; sysimage/fetch.sh downloads it from
  Apple's public servers; its license is Apple's.
- the iPhoneOS 16.5 SDK from github.com/theos/sdks, and theos's cctools (Apple's open-source cctools): the
  kernel's and user space's build tools.
- the phone's firmware (GPU, Wi-Fi, audio DSP, modem, haptics, cameras): the vendor's, pulled from the
  user's own phone (devices/poco-x5-pro/pull-firmware.sh).
- lzfse (Apple, BSD-3-Clause), built by xnuloader/mkidentity.sh when no LZFSE decoder is installed.
- Mesa (for GL=1 images), Procursus and Sileo packages (tools/mk-jb.sh): their own licenses.
